  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: SH1, SH2, unspecified location plan, fire safety strategy, design and access statement. Received: 17/07/2026\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - Notwithstanding the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1 and Class E, Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order), no additional structures/buildings/enclosures within the curtilage of the site shall be carried out\r\nReason:  To protect neighbours' living conditions,  and the character and appearance of the area and to prevent over-intensive use of the site. \r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to commencement of the development of the rear extension hereby approved, the existing rear outbuilding must be removed in its entirety and photographic evidence submitted to the council to demonstrate that the rear garden no longer has a rear outbuilding\r\nReason: To ensure that there is suitable amenity space in the rear garden.  \r\n"
